00:27:08.053 --> 00:27:10.030
of like you deserve this too, bro?

00:27:10.030 --> 00:27:12.130
- So actually that's exactly what I did.

00:27:12.130 --> 00:27:14.000
I said to him, this is a problem.

00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:15.360
Here's the thing, forgetting all that,

00:27:15.360 --> 00:27:16.220
I want to tell you something,

00:27:16.220 --> 00:27:18.440
I looked at him in the eye and I was like,

00:27:18.440 --> 00:27:19.780
you deserve this.

00:27:19.780 --> 00:27:21.600
We have worked together for
years, you deserve this.

00:27:21.600 --> 00:27:23.604
At first, he was like,
what are you talking about?

00:27:23.604 --> 00:27:25.930
And I actually repeated
myself two more times

00:27:25.930 --> 00:27:26.970
and he started to cry.

00:27:26.970 --> 00:27:27.803
- [Gary] That's amazing.

00:27:27.803 --> 00:27:29.430
- And listen,

00:27:29.430 --> 00:27:32.390
I don't know what exactly
happened in that moment.

00:27:32.390 --> 00:27:34.482
But I know that we
embraced at the end of it

00:27:34.482 --> 00:27:35.690
and I know that things changed.

00:27:35.690 --> 00:27:37.083
- [Gary] That's amazing.

00:27:37.083 --> 00:27:38.770
- And I think he just
needed to have someone

00:27:38.770 --> 00:27:40.159
kind of tell him.
- Validate,

00:27:40.159 --> 00:27:41.340
it's validation.

00:27:41.340 --> 00:27:42.970
- Something about it triggered

00:27:42.970 --> 00:27:44.300
and it just taught me something

00:27:44.300 --> 00:27:47.910
about the fact that when people
go through big transitions,

00:27:47.910 --> 00:27:49.190
especially when your identity

00:27:49.190 --> 00:27:51.370
is so tied up in something
that you're building

00:27:51.370 --> 00:27:53.980
